<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:09:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>The Debate</category><title>The Ceuta effect: how far will Europe's anti-migrant backlash go?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260917-the-ceuta-effect-how-far-will-europe-s-anti-migrant-backlash-go</link><description>
As the United States threatens Europe with more tariffs and eyes Greenland, as Russia tests the continent’s resolve over Ukraine, as the planet overheats,  where do citizens sense the biggest threat? In her Wednesday state of the EU speech, the Commission president addressed Ursula von der Leyen going big on manning the borders, literally suggesting new tools to better deal with migration, particularly after July’s run on Ceuta,  where over two days, tens of thousands of mostly Moroccans overran Spain’s North African enclave.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf72f42-b2c1-11f1-b3b4-7922de457103/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T083650Z-1505953259-RC26INA4QD32-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf72f42-b2c1-11f1-b3b4-7922de457103/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T083650Z-1505953259-RC26INA4QD32-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0865d082-b2c1-11f1-ad69-6b9ab73b99dc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:16:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>English village holds symbolic vote to leave UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/english-village-holds-symbolic-vote-to-leave-uk</link><description>
A village in Oxfordshire has held a symbolic referendum to leave the United Kingdom in protest against government plans to house up to 1,200 asylum seekers at a nearby military base. While the vote has no legal force, it highlights wider tensions over the UK's asylum policy and migration debate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce9f6e32-b2a5-11f1-b76e-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-153343-153523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce9f6e32-b2a5-11f1-b76e-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-153343-153523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d42c4c08-b2a5-11f1-a91e-5182ddc2f54d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:17:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Mbappé draws fire from right wing in France, Spain over Ceuta t-shirt controversy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-real-madrid-s-mbapp%C3%A9-draws-criticism-from-far-right-over-ceuta-t-shirt-controversy</link><description>
Real Madrid's French forward Kylian Mbappé is facing mounting criticism by Spanish and French conservative and far-right politicians for partially obscuring a t-shirt supporting residents of Ceuta, Spain's territory bordering Morocco grappling with a migration crisis. Mbappé said he wore the t-shirt rolled up to show solidarity with "all the immigrants who have lost their lives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2260510-b2a9-11f1-8156-39eb0f836866</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:10:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg">© Omar Arnau Cerezo, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Carney pushes Canada-EU ties beyond trade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/carney-pushes-canada-eu-ties-beyond-trade</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney used his address to the European Parliament to signal that Ottawa wants to deepen its partnership with the EU beyond trade, expanding cooperation on energy, AI, space and payment sovereignty, while also seeking to join the Erasmus programme. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating explains how the push reflects Canada's broader strategy to build stronger alliances beyond the United States without seeking to join the EU's single market, even as questions remain over how those ambitions can be turned into concrete action.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31e55368-b2a5-11f1-a3c2-fd76b89f47a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden: Andersson's centre left claims narrow win</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-andersson-s-centre-left-claims-narrow-win</link><description>
Sweden's centre-left opposition, led by Magdalena Andersson, is set to defeat the incumbent right-wing bloc by one seat after nearly all votes were counted in Sunday's election. The narrow result means coalition talks are likely to be challenging, with parliament due to begin the government formation process on September 28.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5531ffa-b297-11f1-af34-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-131830-131930-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5531ffa-b297-11f1-af34-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-131830-131930-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aab972c8-b297-11f1-b100-95518b0bca84</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:22:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ireland to boycott 2027 Eurovision contest over Israel’s participation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-ireland-to-boycott-2027-eurovision-over-israel-s-participation</link><description>
Ireland will boycott the 2027 Eurovision Song Contest for the second year over Israel's participation, the country's public broadcaster RTE said Thursday. Ireland was one of five countries along with the Netherlands, Iceland, Slovenia and Spain to skip Eurovision this year in protest over Israel’s inclusion in the contest, citing its ongoing war on Gaza.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e99dae4-b29b-11f1-878d-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26260416490287.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e99dae4-b29b-11f1-878d-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26260416490287.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4e524dc-b292-11f1-a08a-c3fc3a34c0a7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:26:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e99dae4-b29b-11f1-878d-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26260416490287.jpg">© Valentina Petrova, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden's left-wing opposition wins slim majority in country's national election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-sweden-left-wing-opposition-wins-slim-majority-in-country-national-election</link><description>
Sweden's left-wing opposition won a narrow majority in the country's general election after the vote count ended Thursday, but faces laborious negotiations to form a government. The incumbent prime minister, conservative Ulf Kristersson, announced his resignation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51c978-b28f-11f1-a955-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T220139Z-1787689457-RC2LINAN2WVG-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51c978-b28f-11f1-a955-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T220139Z-1787689457-RC2LINAN2WVG-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5bdfb55c-b28f-11f1-b358-2f46de5ccff5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:02:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51c978-b28f-11f1-a955-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T220139Z-1787689457-RC2LINAN2WVG-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg">© Denis Balibouse, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mark Carney's EU speech highlights Canada's shifting alliances</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament as Ottawa and Brussels deepen ties against a backdrop of strained relations with the United States. FRANCE 24's Doug Herbert explains how the speech illustrates a broader shift in alliances, with a message that, until recently, would more likely have been delivered in Washington than Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fb7a19a-b28a-11f1-b70e-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-120914-121514-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fb7a19a-b28a-11f1-b70e-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-120914-121514-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a47c62f6-b28a-11f1-9a68-51f62954151d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:37:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Canadian PM Mark Carney addresses EU Parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-canadian-pm-mark-carney-addresses-eu-parliament</link><description>
Here's the replay of Mark Carney's address to the European Parliament on Thursday, September 17, after President Donald Trump suggested that allowing Canada to become an associate EU member could be seen as a "hostile act"
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40b1b5ea-b286-11f1-a1ab-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-114608-120859-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40b1b5ea-b286-11f1-a1ab-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-114608-120859-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">455139d6-b286-11f1-b53e-5f3b635e73df</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:04:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>The 'Canaduropean' Union: Canada an associate member of the EU?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260917-the-canaduropean-union-canada-an-associate-member-of-the-eu</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 17: Will Canada become an associate member of the EU? Commissioner Ursula von der Leyen floated the idea in a speech but did not give any details about what it would entail. The press is reacting with scepticism. Also, Le Monde profiles some of the 8,000 people who died during France's summer heatwave. Scientists observe a humpback whale mourning her dead calf for the first time. And Singapore wants to pay citizens to stop scrolling and start reading.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4adb15dc-b26a-11f1-9157-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-17T07-24-33-439Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4adb15dc-b26a-11f1-9157-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-17T07-24-33-439Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a9737b2-b26c-11f1-b446-678dd77152fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:00:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mbappé and Real Madrid teammates face backlash over Ceuta message</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mbapp%C3%A9-and-real-madrid-teammates-face-backlash-over-ceuta-message</link><description>
Real Madrid stars Kylian Mbappé, Vinicius Junior and Ibrahima Konaté have sparked controversy in Spain after partially covering a pro-Ceuta solidarity message on their pre-match T-shirts. The incident has reignited debate over migration, Ceuta's recent migrant crisis and Spain's relationship with Morocco, with politicians and football figures divided over the players' actions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fd08c54-b26d-11f1-a410-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-091149-091339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fd08c54-b26d-11f1-a410-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-091149-091339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5d348ec2-b26d-11f1-b49f-fbeeb0bb8a1f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:10:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Belgium to rule on parole for key figure in 2015 Paris attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/belgium-to-rule-on-parole-for-key-figure-in-2015-paris-attacks</link><description>
Mohamed Bakkali, convicted for coordinating logistics for the 2015 Paris attacks, could be granted parole in Belgium despite receiving a 30-year sentence in France with a 20-year minimum term. Belgian authorities will decide on September 29 whether to release him under electronic monitoring, a prospect that has sparked anger among victims and families, while prosecutors oppose his release.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4b12366-b26c-11f1-ae72-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090928-091117-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4b12366-b26c-11f1-ae72-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090928-091117-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb513e90-b26c-11f1-bf66-476210f4b4ff</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:09:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe and Canada are 'strong, even stronger together', Carney tells European Parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-live-carney-to-speak-after-trump-threatens-more-eu-tariffs-over-canada-s-associate-member-bid</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament on Thursday, welcoming the ambition for Canada to become an EU associate member. "Canada and Europe are stronger, even stronger together," he said, a day after US President Donald Trump threatened new tariffs and to cut trade ties with the EU if Canada's bid succeeds. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7202137a-b280-11f1-9b1c-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T100811Z-851835045-RC2YKNAVHJOI-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7202137a-b280-11f1-9b1c-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T100811Z-851835045-RC2YKNAVHJOI-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">428dd608-b26a-11f1-941f-835f959b1379</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:52:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7202137a-b280-11f1-9b1c-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T100811Z-851835045-RC2YKNAVHJOI-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump threatens EU with tariffs over 'laughable' Canada association plan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-trump-threatens-eu-with-tariffs-over-laughable-canada-association-plan</link><description>
US President Donald Trump has threatened steep tariffs on the European Union if it goes ahead with a proposal to make Canada its first "associate member", a move he described as a possible "hostile act". Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney, who is due to address the European Parliament on Thursday, has been pursuing closer ties with the EU as he seeks to pivot away from the US.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b812582-af80-11f1-89c8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T130451Z-943753214-RC2DINAGWTJK-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-IRELAND.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b812582-af80-11f1-89c8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T130451Z-943753214-RC2DINAGWTJK-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-IRELAND.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb682e28-b263-11f1-b641-77c4cec02d2a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:58:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b812582-af80-11f1-89c8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T130451Z-943753214-RC2DINAGWTJK-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-IRELAND.jpg">© Kylie Cooper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russia to open voting stations at border with Poland, Baltic states</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-live-explosions-kyiv-us-congress-sanctions-moscow</link><description>
Russia said Thursday it would open voting booths at its border points with Poland and the three Baltic states for its three-day parliamentary election that begins on Friday. President Vladimir Putin's party faces no real opposition and is guaranteed to win. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ce19fd4-b2b5-11f1-9613-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T105711Z-1476080514-RC2WKNACW1JU-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ce19fd4-b2b5-11f1-9613-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T105711Z-1476080514-RC2WKNACW1JU-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8dcaad00-b23b-11f1-8f27-a733a75bb45c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 02:08:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ce19fd4-b2b5-11f1-9613-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T105711Z-1476080514-RC2WKNACW1JU-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-ELECTION.jpg">© Ramil Sitdikov, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Putin urges Russians to vote in parliamentary election as show of support for Ukraine war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-putin-urges-russians-to-vote-in-parliamentary-election-as-show-of-support-for-ukraine-war</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir ⁠Putin on Wednesday described voter turnout in the upcoming parliamentary election as a barometer of public support for Russia’s war against Ukraine and urged voters to go to the polls. It will be Russia's first parliamentary election since the Kremlin launched its offensive in February 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d70c6b42-b200-11f1-8501-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259666126716.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d70c6b42-b200-11f1-8501-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259666126716.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e33974bc-b202-11f1-bc70-ab98b003be29</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:47:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d70c6b42-b200-11f1-8501-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259666126716.jpg">© Mikhail Metzel, Sputnik, Kremlin Pool Photo via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>LGBTQ 'a threat to Erdogan's ideal of a strong, masculine state', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lgbtq-a-threat-to-erdogan-s-ideal-of-a-strong-masculine-state-expert-says</link><description>
Turkish courts have jailed more LGBTQ activists and supporters, raising to 62 the number remanded in custody following a weekend crackdown, a legal rights group said on Wednesday. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Koen Slootmaeckers, Reader in International Politics at City St George's, University of London, says that Turkish President Recep Tayyp Erdogan wants to claim "the idea of a strong, masculine state and LGBTQ people are a threat to this ideal".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8e0a398-b205-11f1-b9f2-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-210358-211115-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8e0a398-b205-11f1-b9f2-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-210358-211115-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb66500-b205-11f1-a1e9-135d799d52f5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:39:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden's centre-left opposition wins election, SVT says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-wins-election-svt-says</link><description>
Sweden's centre-left opposition has defeated the incumbent right-wing governing bloc by the slimmest of margins, public broadcaster ​SVT ‌said on Wednesday, after 99% ⁠of the votes in Sunday's parliamentary election had been counted. FRANCE 24's Paul Rhys reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426d5f8a-b202-11f1-9f67-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-203750-204158-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426d5f8a-b202-11f1-9f67-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-203750-204158-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47d28a54-b202-11f1-b1fb-6bfd10007bd4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:21:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>The 28th state? Carney's Canada draws closer to European Union</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260916-the-28th-state-carney-s-canada-draws-closer-to-european-union</link><description>
US president Donald Trump has previously talked about making Canada the 51st state, Now, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is in Europe, and the president of the European Commission has proposed the country ‘associate membership’. In this edition, we ask what that means and how it differs from the close status afforded to Iceland, Norway, Switzerland and the UK – countries which Carney is also visiting ahead of his own Strasbourg speech Thursday before the European Parliament. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d723f5c-b1e2-11f1-88cf-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T083628Z-570247194-RC28KNAPX2ZW-RTRMADP-3-EU-PARLIAMENT-CARNEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d723f5c-b1e2-11f1-88cf-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T083628Z-570247194-RC28KNAPX2ZW-RTRMADP-3-EU-PARLIAMENT-CARNEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e803d2-b1f8-11f1-9a1e-7d47b0bed310</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé falsely accused of lying about his age</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-ivorian-footballer-malick-yalcouy%C3%A9-falsely-accused-of-lying-about-his-age</link><description>
During a Premier League match between Chelsea and Brighton, social media users started spreading rumours that 20-year-old Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé is older than he claims to be. The rumours gained such proportion that the youth club where he trained decided to post photos of Yalcouyé throughout the years. Recently, similar accusations were made against the new Real Madrid striker Yan Diomandé.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43292096-b1ce-11f1-a567-2521ed09eebd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:03:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png">© Premier League</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Former Kosovo president sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-former-kosovo-president-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes</link><description>
Former Kosovo President Hashim Thaci was found guilty of war crimes committed as part of the Kosovo Liberation Army including murder, torture and illegal arrests by a tribunal in The Hague on Wednesday. Thaci was sentenced to 25 ​years in prison alongside fellow former KLA figures who were also found guilty and sentenced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">977d0508-b1ca-11f1-aed3-cdcd2ee68797</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:55:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb01620-b1c9-11f1-8b3a-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CK27L.jpg">© Koen Van Weel, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU chief invites Canada to be first-ever ‘associate member’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-eu-chief-pitches-associate-member-status-for-canada-as-both-seek-to-pivot-away-from-us</link><description>
EU chief Ursula von der Leyen raised the possibility on Wednesday that Canada could become the European Union’s first “associate member” during the annual State of the European Union speech, at which Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney was present. Carney has been pursuing closer ties with the EU as both seek to pivot away from the US.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d19923a-b1e9-11f1-a594-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259438375621.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d19923a-b1e9-11f1-a594-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259438375621.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c3e830c-b1c9-11f1-89e6-c11fd12378d9</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:22:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d19923a-b1e9-11f1-a594-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259438375621.jpg">© Justin Tang, The Canadian Press via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian drone attack on bus kills five in Ukraine's southeast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-russian-drone-attack-on-bus-kills-five-in-ukraine-s-southeast</link><description>
Five people were killed and at least seven more were injured in a Russian drone attack on a passenger bus near the frontline in Ukraine's southeast on Wednesday, the regional governor said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29a8cc46-b19e-11f1-9784-83dc54a6a266</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 07:37:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32a17336-b19c-11f1-8958-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T064924Z-1003482524-RC24KNARF2CC-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Alina Smutko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU chief calls for creation of ‘European Security Council’, backs partnership with Canada</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-live-eu-chief-ursula-von-der-leyen-gives-state-of-the-union-address</link><description>
EU chief Ursula von der Leyen called for the creation of a "European Security Council", with countries including Britain and Ukraine, in her State of the European Union speech to the European Parliament in Strasbourg on Wednesday. Addressing this year's special guest, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, von der Leyen said she wants to open the door for Canada to become the bloc's first associate member.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efea9014-b19f-11f1-97b8-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T071848Z-60195985-RC27KNAAFBWQ-RTRMADP-3-EU-STATEOFUNION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efea9014-b19f-11f1-97b8-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T071848Z-60195985-RC27KNAAFBWQ-RTRMADP-3-EU-STATEOFUNION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9d5ff98-b13e-11f1-be36-99ae0684f658</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 05:20:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efea9014-b19f-11f1-97b8-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T071848Z-60195985-RC27KNAAFBWQ-RTRMADP-3-EU-STATEOFUNION.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France stalls EU Russia sanctions renewal over oligarch de-listing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-stalls-eu-russia-sanctions-renewal-over-oligarch-de-listing</link><description>
European Union envoys have pushed back the expiry of EU Russia sanctions listings by ​seven days until September 22, a spokesperson for the EU's Irish presidency said on Monday, after failing to agree on a six-month renewal. At issue is whether to de-list Russian-Uzbek billionaire Alisher Usmanov. France has joined ​Slovakia in ‌a call to remove him, citing national security concerns, EU diplomats ⁠said. FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba60012-b14e-11f1-aeb9-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-233414-233553-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba60012-b14e-11f1-aeb9-798697543a72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-233414-233553-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9185af8c-b14e-11f1-82a8-4110d51070be</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:46:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO jets down drone over Lithuania as Russian ship fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-jets-down-drone-over-lithuania-as-russian-ship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter</link><description>
NATO fighter jets shot down a drone that entered Lithuanian airspace and Denmark accused a Russian frigate of firing flares at a Danish military helicopter on Tuesday, in incidents that heightened tensions along the alliance’s eastern flank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70fb22aa-b140-11f1-9cce-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T134257Z-1149854285-RC2OJNA2GC74-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE-MINISTERS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70fb22aa-b140-11f1-9cce-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T134257Z-1149854285-RC2OJNA2GC74-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE-MINISTERS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79e24a4c-b140-11f1-a3b3-e9d99f3fc73c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:26:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70fb22aa-b140-11f1-9cce-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T134257Z-1149854285-RC2OJNA2GC74-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE-MINISTERS.jpg">© Janis Laizans, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Analysts call for step-up in response to Russia after Denmark, Lithuania incidents</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/analysts-call-for-step-up-in-response-to-russia-after-denmark-lithuania-incidents</link><description>
The European Union accused Russia on Tuesday of the "reckless" firing of flares at a Danish frigate which, with the shooting down of a drone over Lithuania, heightened the continent's anxiety over the Ukraine-Russia war. Danish analysts are calling for NATO and the EU to step up their response to Russia, according to FRANCE 24's Copenhagen correspondent Trine Villemann.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5eaaa38-b139-11f1-9937-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-203356-203643-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5eaaa38-b139-11f1-9937-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-203356-203643-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb7f7fd2-b139-11f1-96ea-b9649202be76</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:23:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Paris ex-mayor says 'collective failure' led to abuse of children in school care</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-paris-ex-mayor-says-collective-failure-led-to-abuse-of-children-in-school-care</link><description>
Former Paris mayor Anne Hidalgo acknowledged a “collective failure” to protect children on Tuesday as police investigate more than 200 allegations of violence, mistreatment and sexual abuse at the French capital’s state-run nurseries and primary schools for over more than a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/660460fe-b114-11f1-a509-e536a2be234a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8DA6CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/660460fe-b114-11f1-a509-e536a2be234a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8DA6CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d2990da-b114-11f1-880c-4d330ea93e7c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:27:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/660460fe-b114-11f1-a509-e536a2be234a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8DA6CQ.jpg">© Senate, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO downs drone over Lithuania</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-fighter-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania-after-latest-incursion</link><description>
NATO scrambled fighter jets overnight to ​shoot down a drone over Lithuania after the latest incursion on the alliance's eastern flank. In a separate incident, Denmark said a Russian warship fired two emergency flares at a Danish helicopter in the Baltic Sea, adding that the Russian ambassador had been summoned over the "reckless action". Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e289a39e-b111-11f1-ae2a-9bb98dcbfc77/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T081301Z-1741826540-RC2KJNASG13L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e289a39e-b111-11f1-ae2a-9bb98dcbfc77/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T081301Z-1741826540-RC2KJNASG13L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7ae271c-b0ab-11f1-9bc0-97b5e2715bc5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:19:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e289a39e-b111-11f1-ae2a-9bb98dcbfc77/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T081301Z-1741826540-RC2KJNASG13L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-LITHUANIA-DRONE.jpg">© Lithuanian army, Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes</link><description>
Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a838820a-b08f-11f1-b656-b3452f437d0f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:57:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg">© Aurel Obreja, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
